```
Note that the `focus()` method only works on elements that are focusable, such as form fields like input, textarea, select, and button. If you try to focus on an element that is not focusable, it will not work.

Also, keep in mind that focusing on an element can be delayed due to the busy nature of JavaScript execution. If you need to focus on an element immediately, you can use a timeout or a callback function to ensure that the focus is set after the JavaScript has finished executing

